==Location and Uses==
==={{BotW|-}}===
Luminous Stones can be found by breaking [[Luminous Stone Deposit]]s, which can be identified by their glow during the night. They are also dropped by [[Stone Talus (Luminous)|Stone Taluses (Luminous)]] upon their defeat. The [[Kochi Dye Shop]] can use Luminous Stones to make [[Navy Dye]]. Three of them are also required to buy one piece of the [[Radiant Set]] at the [[Gerudo Secret Club]].

If [[Link]] speaks to [[Ledo]] at [[Zora's Domain]], he will explain that he needs more Luminous Stones in order to continue his repairs.<ref name="BotW Ledo"/> He will ask Link to gather 10 Luminous Stones for him, which will initiate the [[Side Quest]] "[[Luminous Stone Gathering]]".<ref name="BotW Ledo 2"/> Upon delivery, Ledo will reward Link with two [[Diamond]]s. Afterwards, Link can bring him 10 Luminous Stones at any time in exchange for one Diamond.<ref name="BotW Ledo 3"/>

The Radiant Set requires Luminous Stones the be upgraded to its first, second, third, and fourth tier at a [[Great Fairy Fountain]].
